--- SURFACE SUMMARY (parity with the web source) -----------------------------------
SavingsSlide is a slide in the Year-in-Review story. The web component is PRESENTATIONAL: it takes
`data: YearReview` as a prop and binds only useTranslation (no fetch). The native port mirrors the
DrivingPerformanceCards / DrivingTab presentational precedent: the WinUI-free SavingsProjection turns a
SavingsSnapshot (parsed from GET /analytics/year-review) + ILocalizer + currency symbol into a render-ready
SavingsDisplay; the SavingsSlide ContentControl is a thin renderer. The view performs no HTTP — the
cache-then-network SavingsSlideSource (operation get_api_v1_analytics_year_review, the generated endpoint
GET /analytics/year-review) owns the read so the surface can render the full state matrix the P2 contract
mandates.

States (every state renders — no hidden surfaces):
  Loading  -> centred slide skeleton (reduce-motion aware; live-region announced)
  Empty    -> TsEmptyState ("No drive data for this year") when the year carries no review payload
  Error    -> TsQueryError + retry (RetryAsync re-runs the load)
  Stale    -> the slide + a "Stale" TsBadge chip + TsDataFreshness + refresh affordance
  Offline  -> the slide + an "Offline" TsBadge chip + cached value + TsDataFreshness(IsError)
  Loaded   -> the populated slide

Slide composition reproduced (all of it):
  1. Hero 💰 (decorative, Narrator-skipped)
  2. "You saved" eyebrow                                  (yearReview.youSaved)
  3. Hero savings figure, count-up 0 -> gas_savings over 1.5s, emerald (TsColorSuccessBrush). The count-up
     reuses the shared Core AnimatedNumberModel (ease-out-quad) and honours MotionPreference.ReduceMotion
     (snaps to the final figure), exactly as the web AnimatedNumber does.
  4. "vs. driving a gas car" caption                      (yearReview.vsGas)
  5. Gas comparison bar  : full red track (TsColorDangerBrush), value = $round(gas_savings+total_charging_cost)  (yearReview.gasCost)
  6. Electric comparison bar : emerald track proportional to total_charging_cost / gasCostEquiv (clamped 0..1)   (yearReview.electricCost)
  7. Coffee note : "That's {round(gas_savings/5)} cups of coffee!"                                               (yearReview.savingsNote, "{0}")

Data / i18n / a11y:
  - gasCostEquiv = gas_savings + total_charging_cost (web parity); figures rounded half-away-from-zero and
    grouped via the shared NumberFormatting (en-US) — the monetary boundary is applied once, in the projection.
  - Every string flows through the ILocalizer facade. All five source keys resolve in the P1/S10 catalog:
    translation.yearReview.{youSaved,vsGas,gasCost,electricCost,savingsNote} all exist in
    Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (savingsNote stored as "That's {0} cups of coffee!"); the chrome reuses
    translation.yearReview.{title,noDriveData,loading} and translation.common.retry (all present). No new keys.
  - AutomationProperties.SetName on the root, the hero number, each comparison bar and the note; decorative
    emoji are AccessibilityView.Raw; reduce-motion honoured by the stagger entrance, the count-up and the
    skeletons.
  - Telemetry: SavingsSlideDiagnostics.RecordViewOpened() emits "view.opened slug=SavingsSlide" (PII-safe —
    never a savings figure / currency amount / VIN / year) per the P1/S11 diagnostics contract.

Tests (SavingsSlideTests.cs, 34 headless cases): the year-review JSON parse adapter (gas_savings /
total_charging_cost, the safe()-coercion of non-finite / non-numeric / numeric-string fields, the HasData
gate, empty / non-object / non-review tolerance), the projection (currency formatting + grouping, custom
currency symbol, the electric fraction incl. zero-gas-cost and over-100% clamp, the cups-of-coffee count, the
interpolated note, and a11y names containing label + value), the cache-then-network result mapper (status
preservation across cached/refreshing/loaded/empty/offline/failure/loading), the view-model per-state matrix
(loading / loaded / loaded-without-data->empty / empty / error / stale / offline / fold), currency-change
reprojection, i18n resolution and PropertyChanged, the repository source request shape (operation id +
year query, vehicle_id filter, empty-body->Empty), and the registration + PII-safe diagnostics.

